@startuml
title NetStrike local network
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam packageTitleAlignment left
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Facilitator / browser" as Browser

package "Exercise network (192.168.0.0/24 | simcorp.test)" as Exercise {
  node "ANSIBLE01\n192.168.0.36\nansible01.simcorp.test\nUbuntu Server 26.04.1 LTS | SSH :22\nOffline-bundle staging\nAnsible playbook runner\nDNS + NTP client" as Ansible
  node "CTRL01\n192.168.0.27\nctrl01.simcorp.test\nUbuntu Server 26.04.1 LTS | SSH :22\nLogical assets: IDP01, HELPDESK01,\nCLOUD01, FILE01 (fixtures)\nController :8443\nDNS + NTP client\nSplunkForwarder" as CTRL
  node "DC01\n192.168.0.70\ndc01.simcorp.test\nWindows | WinRM :5985\nAD DS (NTDS), DNS, W32Time\nSplunkForwarder, Sysmon64" as DC
  node "FIN-WS01\n192.168.0.200\nfin-ws01.simcorp.test\nWindows | WinRM :5985\nDNS + NTP client\nSplunkForwarder, Sysmon64" as WS
  node "SPLUNK01\n192.168.0.234\nsplunk01.simcorp.test\nCyber Range-provided Splunk host\nForwarder receiver :9997" as SPLUNK
}

Browser --> CTRL : HTTPS :8443
Ansible --> CTRL : SSH :22
Ansible --> DC : WinRM :5985
Ansible --> WS : WinRM :5985
Ansible --> SPLUNK

CTRL --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
Ansible --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
WS --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
SPLUNK --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123

CTRL --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997
DC --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997
WS --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997

note bottom of Exercise
  Manifest DNS and NTP servers: 192.168.0.70
  Reverse DNS zone: 0.168.192.in-addr.arpa
  Splunk REST URL: http://splunk01.simcorp.test
  FILE01 is a logical fixture service on CTRL01, not a separate VM.
end note

note bottom
  Based on citef-config/environment.local.json.
  Connections represent manifest endpoints and configured
  services and ports; actual firewall enforcement, participant
  access policy, and external routes require Cyber Range approval.
end note
@enduml
